sentences.text:
10. Let the petitioner be released on bail on furnishing bail bond of Rs. 10,000/- (Ten thousand)
with two sureties of like amount each to the satisfaction of learned Additional District Judge-cum-Special Judge (POCSO), Araria in connection with Mahila P.S. Case No. 33 of 2024 corresponding to Spl. (POCSO) Case No. 47 of 2024, subject to the following conditions:
(i) one of the bailor should be the family member/relative of the petitioner who shall provide official document to show his bona fide;
(ii) the petitioner shall appear on each and every date before the Trial Court failure to do so for two consecutive dates without plausible reason will entail cancellation of his bail bond by the Trial Court itself;
(iii) the petitioner shall appear before the concerned Patna High Court CR. MISC.
No.62948 of 2024(5) dt.11-12-2024 police station every fortnight for next six months to mark his attendance;
(iv) the petitioner shall in no way try to induce or promise or threat the witnesses or tamper with the evidences, failing which the State shall be at liberty to take steps for cancellation of the bail bonds;
Md. Jamil @ Md. Jamil Akhtar vs The State Of Bihar on 11 December, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/157660671/
2 (v) the petitioner shall desist from committing any criminal offence again, failing which the State shall be at liberty to take steps for cancellation of bail bonds.
(Rajiv Roy, J) vinayak/-
U T Md. Jamil @ Md. Jamil Akhtar vs The State Of Bihar on 11 December, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/157660671/
